WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Support-Surge Reliability: your support agent survived the demo; we make sure it survives the outage, the launch day and the invoice.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:15.000
The problem: customer service is the most-bought agent use case; about five percent of production AI requests fail, mostly on rate limits and capacity; and most support agents waste their budget on uncached system prompts.

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:29.000
What we do: surge and rate-limit chaos tests at three, five and ten times your peak; fallback routing and model tiering; a prompt and cache audit; an independent QA harness; cost per resolution under the Governor; vendor-neutral.

4
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:41.000
The deliverable: a surge report showing what customers saw at five times peak, the root cause, the result with the fallback live, containment, cache coverage and cost per resolution. The figures shown are a sample.

5
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:50.000
How the pilot runs: days one and two, access and baseline; days three to six, chaos; days seven to nine, fixes and measurement; day ten, the readout.

6
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Published prices: the two-week pilot is $7,500; the monthly run fee sits in the $8,000 to $15,000 Run and Improve band.

7
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:05.000
Pilots from November 2026 — rainkernel.com or hello@rainkernel.com.
